{"id": "EUVD-2026-87343", "enisaUuid": "df590ed3-8be2-3e41-9899-0baba32f0a0a", "description": "php_openssl_matches_wildcard_name() in ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c underflows the length argument passed to memchr() when a TLS server certificate presents a wildcard name whose literal characters are together longer than the hostname being verified. A malicious server presenting such a certificate makes the PHP client read up to SIZE_MAX bytes past the end of a heap allocation. The path is reachable from any default client stream, because verify_peer_name is enabled by default.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T20:53:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T13:31:31", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-xr7j-rvgx-xq5p"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-91767"], "assigner": "php", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16aa5bb9-fe06-30b4-83fe-9d698dd18d41", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.4.* <8.4.26"}, {"id": "223139e5-9bcc-3d76-895a-6d6dae6e6d83", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.5.* <8.5.11"}, {"id": "2c37eb94-1fe7-373a-8ed0-30198df696fa", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.3.* <8.3.35"}, {"id": "ced0e834-fce4-3574-8a95-ddf0159c72d7", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.2.* <8.2.34"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3c31ca9d-55e8-367a-9edd-4975b30d3e61", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}], "isExploited": false}